# Build context for the root (Railway) Dockerfile.
#
# Docker does NOT read .gitignore, so without this file the whole working tree —
# frontend/node_modules, frontend/.next, backend/.venv, Playwright artefacts and
# any local .env — is uploaded as build context on every build.
#
# Keep `backend/uv.lock`, `backend/pyproject.toml`, `backend/src/` and the
# frontend sources: the Dockerfile copies all of them.

# Secrets — never let a local env file reach a layer.
# These must be `**/`-prefixed: .dockerignore patterns are anchored at the
# context root, so a bare `.env` would miss backend/.env and frontend/.env.local
# entirely. That matters because `COPY frontend/ .` feeds the Next build, and
# next build inlines NEXT_PUBLIC_* from .env.production.local (which outranks
# the .env.local the Dockerfile deletes) into .next/static — which does ship.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/*.pem
**/*.key

# VCS and tooling
.git
.github
.gitignore
.claude

# Python
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
backend/.venv
backend/dist
**/*.egg-info
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache

# Node / Next.js — reinstalled from package-lock.json inside the image
frontend/node_modules
frontend/.next
frontend/out

# Test output. tests/e2e/.auth holds a real JWT — it never reaches the final
# image (only .next/standalone and .next/static are copied out) but it would
# otherwise sit in an intermediate build layer and the build cache.
frontend/playwright-report
frontend/test-results
frontend/tests/e2e/.auth
frontend/tests/e2e/screenshots
frontend/tests/e2e/soak
**/coverage

# Local-only compose layers and docs
docker-compose.override.yml
docs
scratchpad
*.md
!README.md
